<title>UK: Italy's Iveco to close truck plant in UK - paper.</title>
<headline>Italy's Iveco to close truck plant in UK - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iveco, the commercial vehicles arm of Italian carmaker Fiat, will next month announce the closure of its Langley truck plant in southeast England, with the loss of about 500 jobs, the Financial Times reported.</p>
<p>The Iveco factory is near Slough in Buckinghamshire and manufactures the Cargo, Britain best selling truck, in a joint venture with Ford, the FT said.</p>
<p>The news follows an announcement earlier this month by Ford to 1,300 jobs at its UK car plant at Halewood in northwest England. --London newsroom +44 171 542 6762</p>
